Q: How to set persistent values for a TM userscript from elements on the page the script is running in? A: <p>A simple approach is to store the checkbox’s boolean <code>checked</code> state directly. There’s no need to add/remove the <code>checked</code> attribute manually or store <code>&quot;yes&quot;</code>/<code>&quot;no&quot;</code> strings.</p>
<pre><code>const checkbox = document.getElementById('myCheckbox');

checkbox.checked = GM_getValue(checkbox.id, false);

checkbox.addEventListener('change', () =&gt; {
    GM_setValue(checkbox.id, checkbox.checked);
});
</code></pre>
<p>Using <code>false</code> as the default is generally preferable to relying on whether the key exists, because it makes the intended default state explicit. Also, use the <code>checked</code> <strong>property</strong>, not the <code>checked</code> attribute, since the property represents the checkbox's current state.</p>
<p>If the page contains the checkbox dynamically<a href="https://quikconsolees.com/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">,</a> you’d just need to wait until it exists before running this code.</p>
